WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.440
- You know, we could all use a little bit

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:03.600
of encouragement now and again, right?

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:07.800
Well now some of you can get
it 24/7 on a brand new hotline.

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:09.670
Listen to this, this might
be my favorite story.

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:13.660
NPR reports Peptoc is a
hotline that delivers pep talks

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:15.210
from kindergartners.

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:16.740
Two, yeah, I know!

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:18.640
Two teachers named Jessica Martin

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:21.700
and Asherah Weiss put
together this art project

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:24.900
at West Side Elementary school
in Healdsburg, California.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.710
And here, we need to dial a number,

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:29.360
this is the audio you get, listen.

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:30.980
- [Child] Please listen
to the following options

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:33.060
for encouraging messages.

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:36.560
If you're feeling mad,
frustrated, or nervous, press one.

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:38.420
If you need words of encouragement

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:40.590
and life advice, press two.

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:43.423
If you need a Peptoc from
kindergartners, press three.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:45.590
- I know, I know.
- Oh my God!

00:00:45.590 --> 00:00:47.408
- I knew you would love this.

00:00:47.408 --> 00:00:49.240
(Drew squeals)
I know

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:52.060
Before the show I read
this story, so I called,

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:54.640
and I actually, I pushed
three for a Peptoc,

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:57.020
and it was like a group
of, what I think was like,

00:00:57.020 --> 00:00:59.387
30 kindergartners and
they all said in unison,

00:00:59.387 --> 00:01:01.807
"You can do it."

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:07.080
And I believe them! I do
believe them, I can do it.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:08.300
But the teachers say, you guys,

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:10.850
this hotline is so popular,

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:14.020
they've gotten up to 900 calls a minute.

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:15.410
- Oh my gosh.
- Uh huh!

00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:17.210
And you can keep it going.

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:20.030
You go to our website to
find out how you can support

00:01:20.030 --> 00:01:22.320
their hotline costs, but
you can call this number.

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:25.490
I think it's so brilliant
because it shows the kids, like,

00:01:25.490 --> 00:01:28.140
an unconventional way to make
a difference in this world

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:31.390
and that they are important.
(audience applauds)

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:32.223
You know what I mean?

00:01:32.223 --> 00:01:34.350
That they can change grownups.

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:37.230
- Well, here's another
something that I really love.

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:40.950
We love to find little bits
of joy to brighten our day.

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:42.860
And it turns out every single day,

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:44.650
there is something to celebrate,

00:01:44.650 --> 00:01:47.618
because every day's a holiday.

00:01:47.618 --> 00:01:50.535
(audience cheers)

00:01:51.913 --> 00:01:54.950
It's true, it's always
National French Fry Day

00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:57.030
or Best Friends Day or Love Your Dog Day.

00:01:57.030 --> 00:01:57.920
Well, guess what?

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:00.320
This Saturday was National Girl Scout Day.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:01.490
- Aw.
- But we're keeping

00:02:01.490 --> 00:02:03.520
the celebration going.

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:08.040
Please welcome the Daisy Troop
from River Vale, New Jersey,

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:11.033
Isabella, Riley, Ashlyn, and Riley.

00:02:11.919 --> 00:02:16.919
- Hi! Aw!

00:02:18.185 --> 00:02:20.968
Hi, hi, hi! You can put them right here.

00:02:20.968 --> 00:02:24.853
Oh wow! Hi here!

00:02:24.853 --> 00:02:27.289
Here, you can step up right here.

00:02:27.289 --> 00:02:30.122
(audience cheers)

00:02:31.546 --> 00:02:33.310
- Oh, hello girls.

00:02:33.310 --> 00:02:34.715
- Hello.
- Hi, Drew Barrymore.

00:02:34.715 --> 00:02:37.140
- Hi, Drew Barrymore.
- Hi! How are you?

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:39.325
Now, will you please state your name?

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:42.080
- Isabella.
- Isabella.

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:45.030
- Riley Hawks.
- Riley Hawks.

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:47.790
- Ashlyn.
- Ashlyn.

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:50.150
- Riley Newnan.
- Riley Newnan.

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:52.150
It's so nice to meet you.

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:55.370
Interesting that both of
you Rileys have flowers

00:02:55.370 --> 00:02:56.523
in your hair.

00:02:57.560 --> 00:03:01.100
Is that a coincidence, is that
an accident or on purpose?

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:03.050
- Accident.
- We just put it in,

00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:04.080
flowers in our hair,

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:06.400
because it thought it would look nice.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:08.210
- Aw!
- Well, it does.

00:03:08.210 --> 00:03:09.623
- And it does.
- It does.

00:03:10.688 --> 00:03:13.147
(audience applauds)

00:03:13.147 --> 00:03:15.860
- And you put a heart in your hair.

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:16.840
Do you like hearts?

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:18.970
- Yeah.
- I do, too.

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:21.410
And I love your pink bow.
- Thank you.

00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:23.020
- I think it looks so pretty.

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:25.650
Which is your favorite Girl Scout cookie?

00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:27.452
- Thin Mints.
- Mine too.

00:03:27.452 --> 00:03:29.980
- A Thin Mint.
- Oh, well,

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:33.320
I cannot thank you guys
enough for coming here.

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:36.120
Now, I'd like to ask you
one more question, too.

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:39.250
What's your favorite part
of being a Girl Scout?

00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:42.817
- I like to sell cookies.

00:03:42.817 --> 00:03:44.390
(audience laughs)

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:47.580
- And what's your favorite
part of being a Girl Scout?

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:49.520
- Being nice
- Being nice.

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:51.570
- Aw.
- Oh, Riley.

00:03:51.570 --> 00:03:53.790
Ashlyn, what's your favorite?

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:55.700
- Being nice.
- Being nice.

00:03:56.762 --> 00:03:59.845
(audience applauds)

00:04:01.576 --> 00:04:03.530
- So cute.

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:06.340
You guys are this cute and
you brought us cookies.

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:07.250
Okay. You win the day.

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:08.800
You win the day, I have to say.

00:04:10.871 --> 00:04:13.150
- Well thank you so much

00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:15.440
for bringing us these delicious cookies

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:17.770
and all the hard work that you Daisies do

00:04:17.770 --> 00:04:19.050
for your communities.

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:21.850
And Ross and I have a
little something for you.

00:04:21.850 --> 00:04:22.683
- That's right.

00:04:22.683 --> 00:04:25.970
We wanted to award you
these Drew's News badges

00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:28.247
for taking a field trip
to come and see us.

00:04:29.650 --> 00:04:31.480
There's one for you.

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:35.217
- We were wondering if we
could get these patches put

00:04:35.217 --> 00:04:37.870
on your special clothes.

00:04:37.870 --> 00:04:40.150
And also, we're gonna buy a whole bunch

00:04:40.150 --> 00:04:42.330
of your cookies and make your sales go

00:04:42.330 --> 00:04:45.173
woop, through the roof.
(audience cheers)

00:04:45.173 --> 00:04:47.763
How does that sound?
- I've gone over 200 cookies

00:04:47.763 --> 00:04:50.200
that I've sold.
- Good for business.

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:52.220
All right, and we're
also gonna put you guys

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:54.330
and your troop on our website so

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:56.040
that people can buy your cookies

00:04:56.040 --> 00:04:59.470
or figure out how to
support and donate to,

00:04:59.470 --> 00:05:01.933
you know, contribute to the Daisy Troop.

00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:07.470
Well, thank you, Isabella,
Riley, Ashlyn, Riley.

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:10.576
Thank you so much for coming here.

00:05:10.576 --> 00:05:13.270
- You're welcome.
- You beautiful Daisies.

00:05:13.270 --> 00:05:15.670
Okay. This was my favorite.

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:17.230
May I have a Thin Mint?

00:05:17.230 --> 00:05:18.750
Should we all have a cookie?

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:19.639
- Drew Barrymore?
- Yes?

00:05:19.639 --> 00:05:20.472
- You're really beautiful.
- Which kind?

00:05:20.472 --> 00:05:22.060
I'ma have this one.
- Wait, what did you say?

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:24.103
- You're very beautiful.
- I am?

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:25.883
- That's so funny,

00:05:25.883 --> 00:05:28.233
'cause I think the very
same thing about you.

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:30.700
You're so beautiful.

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:32.390
Do you know where it's
the most important place

00:05:32.390 --> 00:05:33.930
to be beautiful?

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:38.570
- Here and home?
- Yes. And inside.

00:05:38.570 --> 00:05:40.370
- Your heart?
- Yes. In your heart.

00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:43.440
Exactly. You all have beautiful hearts.

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:46.050
And this was my favorite
Drew's News we've ever gotten

00:05:46.050 --> 00:05:48.039
to do because of you guys.

00:05:48.039 --> 00:05:50.706
(upbeat music)

